Give this place a try!"},{"review_date":"2021-12-29 01:04:47","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Great breakfast and service. Highly recommend. Staff even took care of noisy transients as they came on by - thank goodness !"},{"review_date":"2021-12-28 19:02:22","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"The wait to be seated was short despite the long line, they work quickly to get your food in front of you. The Customer service at this place is awesome and deserves 5 stars by itself. They are very friendly, prompt, and kept our coffees filled. If you notice the other reviews where Karens were complaining about bad service, were leaving reviews around when covid peaked so don't pay attention to those. I assure you the service is great.

The food is not bad, however it is basic, and safe. Don't get me wrong,  the food tasted fine, it's just that they play it safe which I guess is a good thing so that Karens in SB (There are plenty in this town) don't complain."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"129 E Anapamu St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":true,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":true,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":true,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"no"},"business_stars":3.5,"categories":"Gastropubs, French, Restaurants","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"11:0-22:0","Monday":"11:0-22:0","Saturday":"8:0-22:0","Sunday":"8:0-22:0","Thursday":"11:0-22:0","Tuesday":"11:0-22:0","Wednesday":"11:0-22:0"},"name":"The French Table","review_info":[{"review_date":"2014-05-12 15:42:30","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"THE FRENCH TABLE is no longer in business but there is a new restaurant in it's place called PIANO GASTROLOUNGE.  Great food, great service and the same incredible view.  If you were a fan of The French Table than you should definately come by and try this new menu.  The brunch was very good,  I had a simple soprano omelete which turned out to be not so simple.  It was delicious.  I think it was the carmelized onions that did the trick and made it so unique.  Sit ouside if you can, it is so quiet, beautiful and relaxing."},{"review_date":"2014-03-18 00:09:27","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"This place totally came out of nowhere and it is adorable! 

My server named Dustin was incredibly attentive and kind. 

Plus this world needs more creperies, and The French Table excels in that arena."},{"review_date":"2014-02-21 04:47:01","review_stars":2.0,"review_text":"It's sad to saw but the food was really good but the service was horrid. Working in the food industry I was shocked. My friend and I were ignored by the first waiter who was flirting with a group of girls so we went to the bar. The bartender was busy talking with off the clock staff drinking for free. We were basically ignored. She also made up an excuse not to use our living social deal. Won't be going back. Staff was a joke."}],"state":"CA"}
